{"id":"0d20858d77bcb6066fae8297833715da7da0803c","axis":"silent","repo":"tinacms/tinacms","sha":"0d20858d77bcb6066fae8297833715da7da0803c","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"packages/v4/@tinacms/tinacms/_docs/auth-plugins.md","lines":["@@ -106,6 +106,12 @@ with no login.","   plugin does not attach the token itself."," - The local content and media plugins attach the token the same way. Each","   request reads `store.auth` and calls `getToken()` at the time it is sent.","+- A request to the site's own server carries the token only when the winning","+  auth plugin has a server segment that checks it. The store records this at","+  mount. `useRpcClient` and the local content and media plugins read the","+  same record. A plugin that calls its own backend reads the token through","+  `getToken()` with no such check. `tinaCloud()` is different: it sends","+  TinaCloud its own token and does not read `store.auth`."," - The local Data Layer (`tinaLocalDataLayerVitePlugin`) authorizes the","   content and media requests as the RPC handler does. It answers `401` when","   there is no session, or when the winning auth plugin has no `getSession`.","@@ -122,8 +128,8 @@ with no login."," "," ## TinaCloud"," ","-`tinaCloud({ clientId })` is the reference auth plugin. It provides `auth`","-and `media` from one plugin.","+`tinaCloud({ clientId })` is the reference auth plugin. It provides `auth`,","+`media` and `content` from one plugin."," "," - `login()` signs in the way `https://identity.tinajs.io/v2/auth/config`","   says, as v3 does:","@@ -148,22 +154,28 @@ and `media` from one plugin.","   `no-access`."," - The tokens stay in a closure of the slice. A full reload signs the editor","   out (ADR-023).","-- The media slice of `tinaCloud()` gets its token from the same closure. It","-  never reads the token of another auth plugin, so TinaCloud media needs","-  `tinaCloud()` to keep `auth`.","-- Before a media request, the closure refreshes the token through","+- The media and content slices of `tinaCloud()` send the TinaCloud token to","+  TinaCloud. They do not read `store.auth`, because TinaCloud accepts no","+  token from another auth plugin.","+- Before a request, the closure refreshes the token through","   `https://identity.tinajs.io/oauth/token` when it expires in less than two","   minutes. A refused refresh sets `signed-out` and throws `expired`."," ","-The tokens only ever go to TinaCloud, as in v3. They are tied to the whole","-TinaCloud account, not to one project, so the slice's `getToken()` returns","-`undefined` and the site's own server never receives them. `tinaCloud()` has","-no server segment, so the local Data Layer checks nothing, as in v3, and the","-RPC handler refuses every operation that needs a session.","+The server segment holds `getSession`. It sends the bearer token to the same","+`currentUser` and project endpoints as the slice, and maps the role the same","+way. An account that is not verified, or that TinaCloud refuses, gets no","+session. When TinaCloud cannot be reached, `getSession` throws, so the","+request fails closed. `tinaCloud()` has no `rolePermissions`, so the built-in","+defaults apply.","+","+Because `tinaCloud()` has a server segment, requests to the site's own server","+carry the TinaCloud token. For now that is the token of the whole TinaCloud","+account, not of one project. ADR-023 §7 replaces it with a short-lived,","+project-scoped editor token before v4 ships, once TinaCloud can issue one."," "," ```ts"," defineConfig({","-  plugins: [localContentPlugin(), tinaCloud({ clientId: '<client id>' })],","+  plugins: [tinaCloud({ clientId: '<client id>' })],","   schema: { collections: [] },"," });"," ```","@@ -192,6 +204,11 @@ override with no server segment leaves the RPC handler with no session. For a"," plugin that provides more than one capability, the override replaces `auth`"," only, and the first plugin keeps its other capabilities."," ","+`tinaCloud()` keeps its media and content, but they need its own sign-in.","+With `auth` overridden, each of their operations fails with","+`tinacloud-auth-overridden`. Replace media and content too, or remove the","+override.","+"," ## Not supported yet"," "," - Sign-out on a `401`. A request that carried a token and gets `401` fails,"],"additions":29,"deletions":12,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/v4/@tinacms/tinacms/_docs/media-plugins.md","lines":["@@ -133,17 +133,31 @@ through a symbolic link. It rejects a file name that holds a path separator."," "," ## `tinaCloud()`"," ","-`tinaCloud()` keeps media in TinaCloud. It provides `media` and `auth`, with","-one slice in `slices.media` and one in `slices.auth`. Refer to","-[auth-plugins.md](./auth-plugins.md#tinacloud) for the sign-in flow.","+`tinaCloud()` keeps media and content in TinaCloud. It provides `media`,","+`auth` and `content`, with one slice each in `slices.media`, `slices.auth` and","+`slices.content`. Refer to [auth-plugins.md](./auth-plugins.md#tinacloud) for","+the sign-in flow.","+","+`tinaCloud()` provides `content`, so it cannot sit next to","+`localContentPlugin()`. Swap all of it for the local plugins in local","+development:"," "," ```ts","-import { defineConfig, localContentPlugin, tinaCloud } from '@tinacms/tinacms';","+import {","+  defineConfig,","+  localContentPlugin,","+  localMediaPlugin,","+  tinaCloud,","+} from '@tinacms/tinacms';","+","+const clientId = import.meta.env.TINA_PUBLIC_CLIENT_ID;","+const isLocal = !clientId;"," "," export default defineConfig({","   plugins: [","-    localContentPlugin(),","-    tinaCloud({ clientId: '<client id>' }),","+    ...(isLocal","+      ? [localContentPlugin(), localMediaPlugin()]","+      : [tinaCloud({ clientId })]),","   ],","   schema: { collections: [] },"," });","@@ -153,8 +167,10 @@ export default defineConfig({"," |---|---|"," | `clientId` | The client ID of the TinaCloud project. |"," ","-The media slice gets the token from the auth slice of the same plugin. Before","-the editor signs in, each operation fails with `unauthorized`.","+The media and content slices send the TinaCloud token from `tinaCloud()`'s own","+sign-in. Before the editor signs in, each operation fails with","+`unauthorized`. With `auth` overridden, each operation fails. Refer to","+[auth-plugins.md](./auth-plugins.md#swap-a-provider)."," "," The slice supplies `rename`, `features.search`, `features.extensionFilter` and"," a `features.maxSize` of 100 MB. `resolveUrl` gives a CDN URL, and a size adds"],"additions":24,"deletions":8,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/v4/@tinacms/tinacms/_docs/media.md","lines":["@@ -17,9 +17,13 @@ In the `plugins: [ ... ]` declaration a mediaPlugin needs to be defined."," Note: the `media` capability is a single-provider capability; so we can only ever have 1 active  media provider. An example of how this is used in an app could be: "," "," ```ts","+const clientId = import.meta.env.TINA_PUBLIC_CLIENT_ID;","+const isLocal = !clientId;","+"," plugins: [","-  localContentPlugin(),","-  isLocal ? localMediaPlugin() : tinaCloud({ clientId }),","+  ...(isLocal","+    ? [localContentPlugin(), localMediaPlugin()]","+    : [tinaCloud({ clientId })]),"," ]"," ```"," "],"additions":6,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/v4/@tinacms/tinacms/src/core/auth/contract.ts","lines":["@@ -65,7 +65,8 @@ export class AuthError extends Error {"," "," // ADR-023 §4/§5: the provider drives login and owns the token. The token stays in"," // memory, never in slice state or localStorage, and getToken refreshes it.","-// getToken is the token the site's own server receives; undefined sends none.","+// getToken is the token for the CMS backend; undefined sends none. The site's own","+// server receives it only when the auth plugin has a server segment."," // ADR-008: `roles` gate the UI only. The server check is the security boundary."," export type AuthSlice = (","   | { status: 'signed-in'; user: AuthUser; roles: string[] }"],"additions":2,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/v4/@tinacms/tinacms/src/core/auth/slice.ts","lines":["@@ -49,9 +49,18 @@ export const authTokenOf = async (","   state: TinaStoreState"," ): Promise<string | undefined> => authSliceOf(state)?.getToken();"," ","-export const authHeadersOf = async (","+// The store sets this on the auth namespace at mount. A site's server gets the","+// token only when the auth plugin has a server segment that checks it.","+export const SITE_TOKEN_FLAG = 'sendsTokenToSite';","+","+export const siteAuthTokenOf = async (","+  state: TinaStoreState","+): Promise<string | undefined> =>","+  state.auth?.[SITE_TOKEN_FLAG] === true ? authTokenOf(state) : undefined;","+","+export const siteAuthHeadersOf = async (","   state: TinaStoreState"," ): Promise<Record<string, string>> => {","-  const token = await authTokenOf(state);","+  const token = await siteAuthTokenOf(state);","   return token ? { authorization: `Bearer ${token}` } : {};"," };"],"additions":11,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/v4/@tinacms/tinacms/src/core/content/contract.test.ts","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@","+import { describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';","+import { toFieldAddress } from '../field/address';","+import { ContentError, type ContentErrorCode } from './contract';","+","+const CODES: ContentErrorCode[] = [","+  'unauthorized',","+  'forbidden',","+  'not-found',","+  'branch-not-found',","+  'not-indexed',","+  'validation',","+  'network',","+  'backend-failure',","+];","+","+describe('ContentError', () => {","+  it.each(CODES)('gives %s a message and keeps the detail', (code) => {","+    const error = new ContentError(code, 'Why.');","+    expect(error).toBeInstanceOf(Error);","+    expect(error.name).toBe('ContentError');","+    expect(error.code).toBe(code);","+    expect(error.message).not.toBe('');","+    expect(error.detail).toBe('Why.');","+  });","+","+  it('keeps the field errors of a validation failure', () => {","+    const fieldErrors = { [toFieldAddre